From 5a6535ca208a7e6c3d8de35c2472fad63ea3dce1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yami <yami@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:23:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] input: bindings by the Latin layout's key in non-Latin
 layouts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

raw_latin_sym_or_raw_current_sym returned the current layout's sym whenever it was ASCII. Russian
(and Ukrainian, Belarusian…) types «.» on the key where US has «/», so with Russian active Mod+/
did nothing and Mod+. fired instead. A non-Latin layout now takes the sym of the first Latin
layout for the same key, punctuation included; Latin layouts keep their own labels as before.
